Source: droidloom
Section: misc
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Droidloom packaging <packaging@droidloom.invalid>
Build-Depends: cargo (>= 1.85), rustc, pkg-config, debhelper-compat (= 13)
Standards-Version: 4.7.0
Rules-Requires-Root: no
Homepage: https://github.com/denialwm/droidloom
Vcs-Git: https://github.com/denialwm/droidloom
Vcs-Browser: https://github.com/denialwm/droidloom

Package: droidloom-runtime
Architecture: @ARCH@
Depends: droidloom-image (= @VERSION@), libc6, libgcc-s1, libgbm1, libxkbcommon0, libwayland-client0, libdrm2, libegl1, libpipewire-0.3-0t64 | libpipewire-0.3-0, pipewire, libvulkan1, libgl1-mesa-dri, systemd, polkitd | policykit-1, util-linux, e2fsprogs, iproute2, nftables, iptables, adb, tar, zstd
Recommends: @IMAGE_RECOMMENDS@
Suggests: wireplumber
Description: Android applications in native Wayland windows (host runtime)
 Droidloom runs Android on the host as a private cell and presents each
 Android window as an ordinary Wayland surface, handled by the desktop's own
 compositor.
 .
 This package carries the privileged cell daemon (droidloomd), the
 droidloomctl lifecycle command, the presenter (droidloom-wayland), the audio,
 GPU, device and application services, the systemd units, the polkit action
 and the portable cell recipe. Android itself comes from droidloom-image and
 droidloom-base.

Package: droidloom-image
Architecture: @ARCH@
Depends: droidloom-base (= @BASE_VERSION@), libc6, libgcc-s1
Description: Android applications in native Wayland windows (Android runtime)
 Droidloom runs Android on the host as a private cell and presents each
 Android window as an ordinary Wayland surface, handled by the desktop's own
 compositor.
 .
 This package carries the Android system services Droidloom builds from
 source, the Mesa and ANGLE libraries the cell loads, the framework images and
 the vendor partition. It is installed and replaced as one unit together with
 droidloom-runtime.

Package: droidloom-base
Architecture: @ARCH@
Description: Android applications in native Wayland windows (Android partitions)
 Droidloom runs Android on the host as a private cell and presents each
 Android window as an ordinary Wayland surface, handled by the desktop's own
 compositor.
 .
 This package carries the Android partitions that change only with the pinned
 Android base (system, system_ext and product), so a runtime or vendor update
 need not republish them. It is published only when those partitions change
 and never carries user data.
